Lifecycle defects confirmed from source excerpts:
1. RTW88WCLController::releaseNativeResources currently releases the RX adapter, recycles staged RX packets, and destroys Skywalk queues/pools before attempting the PCI bus-master fence. If the fence fails, the method returns after those resources have already been destroyed.
2. RTW88WCLController::free calls releaseNativeResources but ignores whether it completed. It then releases _workLoop and calls super::free even when cleanup returned early, potentially leaving children or callbacks tied to a freed controller/workloop.
3. RTW88WCLPCIBackend::free disables bus mastering as a last resort but does not read back the PCI command bit before closeResources releases DMA descriptors and the MMIO/PCI state.
4. setRadioRunning(true) can return NotReady after a partial PCI enable. The Stage24 source did not demonstrate rollback/readback of bus mastering in that failure branch.
Current queue objects remain explicitly unregistered; the start path contains a publication fence and fails start until native Skywalk registration, rings, packet metadata and teardown are ready.

